# Caqli web — Vite / browser
#
# 1) Copy this file to `.env.local` (same folder). That file is gitignored — put real values ONLY there.
# 2) Do NOT paste secrets into `.env.example` — this file is usually committed to git.

# Primary T3 server (pairing + WebSocket). In dev, leave unset to use the Vite dev server proxy.
# VITE_HTTP_URL=
# VITE_WS_URL=

# --- Hosted sign-in (Supabase email magic link) — optional ---
# Only needed if you want /welcome + magic link instead of only /pair.
# Free Supabase projects include Email auth (magic link / OTP). No extra subscription for that.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL must be your project API URL, like:
#   https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
# (Find it: Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API → Project URL.)
# NOT the dashboard link and NOT localhost — it always ends with .supabase.co
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = “anon” / “public” key from the same API page (safe in frontend).
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_anon_key_here

# In Supabase: Authentication → URL configuration
# Set Site URL to match where the app runs, e.g. http://localhost:5733
# Under “Redirect URLs”, add exactly:
#   http://localhost:5733/auth/callback
# (Our Vite default port is 5733 — if yours differs, use that port.)
#
# You can ignore “OAuth Server (BETA)” for Caqli magic link — that is a different feature.
# Enable / use “Email” under Sign In / Providers if magic link is not working.

# --- Dogfood access gate (invite-only) ---
# Default when Supabase is set: invite mode (only allowlisted emails).
# VITE_HOSTED_ACCESS_MODE=open
# VITE_HOSTED_ACCESS_MODE=invite
# VITE_HOSTED_ALLOWLIST_EMAILS=you@company.com,teammate@company.com
